    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Jessica Caloza is a Democratic member of the California State Assembly, representing the 52nd District since 2024, and previously served as a Los Angeles Public Works Commissioner and deputy chief of staff to the state attorney general. In the Assembly, she wrote AB 1650 to increase transparency around ICE's use of unmarked vehicles. She also proposed a constitutional amendment to add a second voting student regent at the University of California. Her campaign says she supports lowering the cost of living, building affordable housing, strengthening public education, and protecting reproductive freedom. She passed bills addressing property-tax welfare exemptions for community land trusts and reserve accounts for common interest developments.",
